in and the peer's log \\\"\n \\\"reached the same index, so the entry first committed alone later became a quorum commit of the committed configuration. The durability hazard is \\\"\n \\\"therefore confined to the interval between that lone commit and a successful restart with the peer reachable.\\\")\n if c.startswith('The phantom configuration exists only in memory') else c for c in new['counterevidence']]\nnew['limitations']=[(\\\"Recovery was measured in one configuration only: the restart led again and the peer caught up, with the peer reachable throughout. The case where \\\"\n \\\"the node never restarts, or restarts while the peer is unreachable, is the interval in which the lone commit stays unsupported and was not exercised.\\\")\n if l.startswith('Recovery after a restart') else l for l in new['limitations']]\nnew['joint_history']=(\\\"Receipt adbbb5d29a08477b9dbbd7da187f7f26 is the third revision of 6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-experiment under this question and \\\"\n \\\"replaces the restart phase of the second revision, whose transport wiring was defective. The failed change, the phantom configuration and the lone commit \\\"\n \\\"are identical across the first and third receipts, so the events describe the same subject; the third adds a valid restart observation.\\\")\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Fold the corrected restart receipt into the phantom-configuration account: with the transport wired back to the peer, the restarted node \\\"\n  \\\"led again under the log-derived configuration and the peer's log reached index 5, so the entry first committed alone became a quorum commit. The void \\\"\n  \\\"restart attempt is no longer cited, the memory-only counterevidence becomes a measured repair bound, and the untested never-restarted case is stated as the \\\"\n  \\\"remaining interval.\\\"),\n 'interpretations':[new]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('ce',len(new['counterevidence']),'lim',len(new['limitations']))\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
